{"id": "mm7214a4", "attempt": "read", "status": "ok", "message_id": "msg_011Cg7nGQ46ixj7nBxejyQkX", "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "stop_reason": "end_turn", "error_kind": "", "errors": [], "usage": {"input": 34059, "write_1h": 0, "write_5m": 0, "cache_read": 0, "output": 4923}, "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"id\":\"mm7214a4\",\"reader\":{\"model\":\"prod\",\"reader_id\":\"prod\",\"role\":\"judgment\"},\"data_focus\":{\"v\":\"yes\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Maintaining continuous airflow through school buildings during active hours was the most frequently reported strategy by school districts (50.7%)\"}]},\"outcome_types\":[{\"v\":\"binary/categorical\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"33.9% of school districts reported replacement or upgrade of heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems\"}]}],\"analytic_depth\":[{\"v\":\"summary\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"None of the ventilation strategies examined was reported by >51% of school districts.\"}]},{\"v\":\"comparison\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"Implementation of ventilation improvements varied by school district U.S. Census Bureau region, geographic locale, and poverty level.\"}]}],\"procedures\":[],\"comparison\":{\"framework\":\"group\",\"scale\":null,\"referent\":null,\"across\":[\"poverty level\",\"NCES locale\",\"U.S. Census Bureau region\"],\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"Implementation of ventilation improvements varied by school district U.S. Census Bureau region, geographic locale, and poverty level.\"},{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"High-poverty school districts reported implementation of the highest percentage of strategies.\"}]},\"inference\":{\"v\":\"none\",\"method_stated\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"primary_measures\":[{\"v\":\"percentage\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"Number and percentage of K–12 public school districts surveyed* about COVID-19 prevention strategies (N = 8,410)\"}]}],\"regression_fields\":null,\"public_health_question\":{\"v\":\"What ventilation improvement strategies did U.S. K–12 public school districts report, and did implementation differ by region, locale and district poverty level?\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"CDC examined reported ventilation improvement strategies among U.S. K–12 public school districts using telephone survey data collected during August–December 2022.\"}]},\"conditions\":[{\"v\":\"COVID-19\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"To reduce school transmission of SARS-CoV-2, K–12 public school districts implemented ventilation improvements\"}]}],\"study_design\":[{\"v\":\"cross-sectional\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"although this study used a census-based approach to survey all U.S. K–12 public school districts\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"other survey\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"repeatedly surveyed school district office staff members by telephone during August 8–December 29, 2022\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"MCH Strategic Data Survey\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"table 1\",\"q\":\"MCH Strategic Data Survey.\"}]},{\"v\":\"Small Area Income Poverty Estimates (SAIPE), 2021\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"Poverty levels were based on the 2021 SAIPE for school-aged children living in poverty\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"US national\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Ventilation Improvements Among K–12 Public School Districts — United States, August–December 2022\"}]},\"vaccine_outcome_type\":null,\"equity\":{\"level\":2,\"level_reason\":\"District poverty tertiles are a stratifier and the Discussion speaks of socioeconomic disparities, but percentages are only set side by side with no computed difference or ratio, so the level is capped at 2.\",\"level_confidence\":\"medium\",\"level_alternative\":{\"level\":3,\"reason\":\"The article frames 'socioeconomic disparities' and interprets the high-poverty difference with an explanation (federal funding experience), though no contrast is quantified.\"},\"dimensions\":[{\"v\":\"SES\",\"role\":\"stratifier\",\"ses_components\":[\"school district poverty level (SAIPE)\"],\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"as the percentage of children and adolescents aged 5–17 years experiencing poverty within a school district, grouped into tertiles.\"}]},{\"v\":\"age\",\"role\":\"population\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"implemented by kindergarten through grade 12 (K–12) schools to stay open for safe in-person learning.\"}]}],\"determinants_of_health\":{\"v\":\"prioritization of high-poverty districts and experience applying for federal funding\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"these districts might have been prioritized and might have more experience applying for federal funding\"}]},\"equity_action\":{\"v\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_measurement\":\"SES is an area measure (district SAIPE poverty tertiles). NCES locale of school districts is rurality of non-human units and region is geography, so neither is treated as an SPD; 28%–60% of responses were unknown or missing.\"},\"groupwise\":[{\"across\":[\"SES\"],\"n_groups\":3,\"ordered\":true,\"assessment\":\"side by side\",\"resolves_to_finer\":false,\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"High-poverty school districts more frequently reported each of the four ventilation improvements in most schools than did low- and mid-poverty school districts\"}]}],\"uncertain_fields\":[\"equity.level\",\"equity.dimensions\",\"groupwise\"],\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"notes\":\"Design inferred as cross-sectional from the census-based telephone survey; no design is named. All comparisons are descriptive percentages with no tests or CIs. Rurality was excluded as an SPD because the units are school districts; a reader treating locale as rurality would add a 4-group side-by-side groupwise entry.\",\"view_issues\":\"Discussion says rural districts less frequently reported HVAC upgrades than other locales, but Table 2 shows rural 33.8% vs town 31.2%. 'Differences' are asserted with no test. The R version given (1.4.1106) is an RStudio version.\"}", "type": "text"}]}